{
  "_doc": [
    "THE PLANE-HOOK ISOMORPHISM ALLOWLIST — the accepted per-hook asymmetries across the installed",
    "planes, read by crates/busbar/tests/plane_isomorphism.rs (Assertion I2 of",
    "docs/design/BUSBAR-1.6.0.md THE DESIGN, §1).",
    "",
    "The test REFLECTS the actual Some/None of each installed &'static PlaneDecl (it does not re-read",
    "this file to decide the matrix). For every hook field where one plane is Some and a sibling is",
    "None, the None is FORBIDDEN unless it is declared here AND the named capability maps to a real",
    "cell in qa/capability-equality.json for that plane's ledger column(s). An undeclared asymmetric",
    "None is RED (a plane silently not doing what a sibling does). A declared row that is NOT actually",
    "an asymmetric None on the live decls is also RED (a stale exemption). Over- and under-count both",
    "fail, so the file cannot drift from the decls.",
    "",
    "Each row: { field, planes_none[], capability, reason }. `field` is a PlaneDecl Option hook;",
    "`planes_none` are the installed plane keys whose None is legitimate; `capability` is the",
    "qa/capability-equality.json capability whose cell contextualizes the absence; `reason` is the",
    "one-line argument a reviewer can disagree with. Voice is NOT installed in the binary/this test",
    "target (off-default, feature-gated), so its skeleton asymmetries are governed by the no-deferral",
    "gate + the ledger's voice pin, not by this reflection — see the test header.",
    "",
    "P3 DEL-MCP (ARCHITECT 2026-10-05): the MCP plane is served through its memory-ABI door alone and",
    "installs no PlaneDecl, so it left the reflected set. The six on_swap / parse_endpoint /",
    "lower_endpoint rows (asymmetric only against MCP's Some) and the `mcp` entries of the start /",
    "card_signing_domain / card_kid_prefix rows were struck as stale in the same commit."
  ],
  "asymmetries": [
    {
      "field": "routes",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the LLM plane is the fallback data-plane: it answers on the neutral completion ingress, not plane-mounted routes, so it declares no route hook"
    },
    {
      "field": "admin_routes",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the LLM `pools:` section is not a 1.5.3 named-definition-map, so the plane has no per-registration admin surface to mount"
    },
    {
      "field": "openapi",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the LLM plane contributes no plane-owned OpenAPI path document; its surface is the core completion API, not a plane fragment"
    },
    {
      "field": "hydrate",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "disposition",
      "reason": "the LLM plane holds no durable per-registration state to restore on boot; there is nothing to hydrate"
    },
    {
      "field": "start",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "disposition",
      "reason": "the LLM plane runs no long-lived start-time task; only the A2A server plane starts a background loop"
    },
    {
      "field": "config_validate",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the LLM `pools:` grammar is validated by core's pool config path, not by a plane-owned config_validate hook"
    },
    {
      "field": "registry_contains",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the LLM plane keeps no named-registration registry to answer containment on; its pools are core-owned config"
    },
    {
      "field": "reresolve_gates",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "trust-pinning",
      "reason": "the LLM plane pins no per-peer artifact, so there are no container gates to re-resolve on a swap"
    },
    {
      "field": "retain_verify_gates",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "trust-pinning",
      "reason": "the LLM plane retains no verify gates because it holds no pinned peer artifacts across generations"
    },
    {
      "field": "default_section",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the LLM `pools:` section is core-owned config today, so the plane supplies no default section object"
    },
    {
      "field": "build_runtime",
      "planes_none": [
        "a2a"
      ],
      "capability": "catalogue",
      "reason": "the A2A plane is delegation-only today and builds no per-generation runtime object; LLM and MCP each build one"
    },
    {
      "field": "card_signing_domain",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "trust-pinning",
      "reason": "agent-card signing identity is an A2A-only capability; the LLM plane issues no signed card"
    },
    {
      "field": "card_kid_prefix",
      "planes_none": [
        "llm"
      ],
      "capability": "trust-pinning",
      "reason": "the card key-id prefix is part of A2A-only agent-card signing; the LLM plane mints no card key"
    }
  ]
}
